<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33691" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑλί̆κ-η</span></b> , ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕλιξ</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>winding</i>: hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b>
			<i>the constellation of the Great Bear</i>, from its <i>revolving
				round</i> the pole, <i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				37
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				3.1195
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>convolution</i> of a spiral shell, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				524b12
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PA</u>
				680a22
			</span></i>,al.; of the bowels, ib.<i><span class="en">
				682a15
			</span></i>; of the ear, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>GA</u>
				781b15
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> in Arcadia,
				<i>crack willow, Salix fragilis</i>, from its pliant nature,
				<i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				3.13.7
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
